arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a shipment tracking Blazor Web App. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-ceb3813eed0d49889c0fc5459ae01a8b/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. It is a two-project solution:

- **Server project**: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/` 
- **Client project**: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`

The app uses **Interactive Auto, Global** render mode. Identity auth is configured with SQLite. The target framework is `net11.0`.

## Key Architecture Rules (Auto mode)

- All interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project.
- Interactive components CANNOT access DbContext directly — must use HTTP APIs.
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient there, and with direct DB access on server.
- Register matching services in both `Program.cs` files.

## What to Implement

### 1. Shared Models in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Service Interface in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus);
}
```

### 3. Client-side HttpClient Implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ClientShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ClientShipmentService(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", newStatus);
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side EF Entity

Create `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(20)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public int Status { get; set; }

    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(500)]
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 5. Update ApplicationDbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add Shipments DbSet and seed data:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();

    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder builder)
    {
        base.OnModelCreating(builder);

        builder.Entity<Shipment>().HasIndex(s => s.TrackingNumber).IsUnique();

